        "original_id": "003472c2-37c9-5e53-8d26-6b773ad15474",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, Mike Posner, Lil Wayne, Rick Ross, DJ Khaled, Big Sean\n- Groups: B2K, The Olympicks, Triple C's\n- Projects: Detroit (mixtape), I Am Not a Human Being, Teflon Don, Custom Cars & Cycles, Kiss The Ring\n- Places: Detroit, Michigan\n- Topics: music careers, hip-hop production, vocals, music videos\n\nFacts:\n- Jhené Aiko began her music career by contributing vocals and appearing in several music videos for the R&B group B2K.\n- The Olympicks originated in Detroit, Michigan.\n- The Olympicks have worked on hip-hop projects including Lil Wayne's \"I Am Not a Human Being,\" Rick Ross' \"Teflon Don,\" Triple C's \"Custom Cars & Cycles,\" DJ Khaled's \"Kiss The Ring,\" and Big Sean's \"Detroit\" mixtape.\n- Big Sean's \"Detroit\" mixtape includes American singers Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, and Mike Posner.",
